menu "strpp Configuration"

	config STRPP_THREAD_DEFAULT_STACK_BYTES
		int "Default stack size for strpp::Thread (bytes)"
		default 4096
		help
			Used by strpp's Thread class (include/thread.h) whenever a
			Thread is constructed without an explicit
			ThreadParams::stackBytes override. Converted to StackType_t
			words and passed to xTaskCreate() as the usStackDepth
			argument.

	config STRPP_THREAD_DEFAULT_PRIORITY
		int "Default FreeRTOS task priority for strpp::Thread"
		default 1
		range 0 24
		help
			Passed to xTaskCreate() as the uxPriority argument for every
			strpp::Thread (there is currently no per-Thread override for
			this - see include/thread.h).

	config STRPP_MAX_THREAD
		int "Maximum concurrent strpp::Thread instances (0 = unbounded)"
		default 0
		help
			If non-zero, this preallocates the Thread registry (the
			Array<Thread*> in src/thread.cpp) to this capacity once at
			startup, avoiding reallocation and reducing the out-of-memory
			hazard on constrained targets. It is not currently enforced
			as a hard limit. Leave at 0 to let the registry grow
			dynamically instead.

	config STRPP_THREAD_LOCAL_SLOTS
		int "Thread-local storage slots strpp may claim"
		range 1 16
		default 4
		help
			The most slots the program may claim for ThreadLocal objects
			(include/thread_local.h). strpp claims two: the error buffer,
			and the one shared by every thread's MessageQueue::mine()
			inbox; claiming more than this stops the program at startup. Set
			FREERTOS_THREAD_LOCAL_STORAGE_POINTERS to at least this plus
			one - ESP-IDF keeps index 0 - or the build fails. Each slot
			costs a pointer in every task.

endmenu
